REP027 Safeguarding Return — Architecture Reference
Nov 16, 2026 · @piyush
REP027 is a 17-section, 56-question GDS-style online return that one Spring Boot service (dcp-sca-rep3-service) drives end to end: Drools decides every branch, skip and validation; answers live as JSON in S3; and per-section progress lives in MySQL. This document describes how those parts fit, based on the code snapshots in this project (main service snapshot dated 1 July 2026) plus the team's working notes. Where a detail comes only from notes and not from a snapshot, it says so.
1. Purpose and business context
REP027 is the FCA's Safeguarding Return (SUP 16 Annex 29BR). Payment and e-money institutions use it to report how they safeguarded client funds over the reporting period: methods used, balances, where funds were held, reconciliations, record keeping and CASS breaches.
