4. Data model and storage
One return is spread over three stores that must agree: the answer JSON and the task JSON in S3, and one journey row per section in MySQL. The FIRM_DATA_ITEM row (owned by DIMS) is the parent record that ties them together through FIRM_DATA_ITEM_ID.
MySQL (FDC_APP_METADATA schema)
FIRM_DATA_ITEM holds one row per return instance. Columns used by REP027: FIRM_DATA_ITEM_ID, FIRM_REFERENCE_NO, HANDBOOK_REF_NO (REP027), REPORTING_PERIOD_START, REPORTING_PERIOD_END, SUBMISSION_DUE_DT, COMPLETION_STATUS (for example NO DATA, DRAFT, Ready to Submit, SUBMITTED), FIRM_DATA_ITEM_DATA (S3 path of the answer JSON), SUBMISSION_METHOD, REPORTING_BASIS, FLOW_CURRENCY, UPDATED_BY, UPDATED_DATE_TIME.
FIRM_DATA_ITEM_EXT holds the form journey, one row per section per return. The table is shared with other task-list returns: the 1 Oct 2025 sample also shows CreditBroking, DebtAdjustingDebtCounselling and ProvidingCreditInformationServices task groups.
