Answer JSON shape
The answer JSON mirrors the XSD, with three extra blocks the XML never sees:
• REP027-SafeguardingReturn holds the answers, with @xmlns, @currency and @units attributes and one object per section (for example SafeguardingInstInfo, SafeguardingRelevantFunds.SegregatedRelevantFunds[]).
• Reference[] holds one entry per section (sectionName) with questions[]. Each question carries id (page ID), questionId, xmlPath, status (for example updated), type (table for Sections 4 and 12) and nextqid.
• validationErrorResponse and EnabledQIds hold accumulated errors and cross-section enablement.
Task JSON shape
tasks.json has one SafeguardingReturn root with sectionList[17]. Each entry has id ("1 to 4"), name and xmlPath (the section path), status, startQID, enabled, hasSubsections, resumePageId, checkYourAnswer, and questionType: table for Sections 4 and 12. The UI builds the task list and its resume links from this file alone.
