QuestionsMap and DependencyMap
QuestionsMap is the single registry that turns IDs into XPaths, section names, page names and S3 form-builder paths. It has three kinds of entry, told apart by constructor:
• 2-argument entries (code, xPath) are containers such as "Section 4 - Subsection 3.1". They are grouping labels, not questions, and must be filtered out before anything is written to the database.
• 3-argument entries add the page (fileName), for example ("4A", "...SafeguardingInstInfo.AuditorReportDate", "4").
• 4-argument entries add csvName for questions that accept CSV upload.
Lookups used everywhere: getSectionNameByQuestionId, getXpathByQuestionId, getS3FilePathByQuestionId, getCsvNameByQuestionId, and getSectionNameByQIdBasedOnFlowType, which returns Special1 for 1A–4C, Special2 for 5A and Special3 for 31A when the flow is guidedPermission.
DependencyMap records each question's parent questions, for example 3A ← 2A, 4A ← 2A, 3A, 6A ← 5A, 11AA ← 6A, 6B, 11A ← 11AA, 13A ← 12A. SaveAndContinueService uses it two ways: collectDependentsForMultipleIds walks dependents transitively from the questions just answered, and findControllers finds the parent questions when it builds Reference entries for newly enabled questions.
6. Drools rules engine
Drools is the single source of truth for form behaviour: every branch, skip, visibility change, cross-section enablement and business validation is a rule, and the Java layer only applies the results. The active rules file is Updated drool 16 june (package rulesREP027_v1), running on Drools 7.74.0.Final today.
