Two KIE sessions are defined in kmodule.xml: ksession-rules-REP027_v1 for online saves and ksession-rules-REP027-xml-v1 for XML uploads (branching XML). KieValidationService reads kmodule.xml at startup and creates each session once to warm the container, then hands out a new KieSession per request from the classpath KieContainer.
How Java calls the rules
ApplicationValidationImpl.runAgendaGroupValidationRule(request, dpInfo, questionIds, completedQuestionIds) in dcp-lib-functional-core does the work:
1.  Opens a new session, sets the error globals and inserts the merged SaveREP027DataItemRequest as the only fact.
2.  For each question ID on the page, resets the per-question globals, then focuses and fires these groups in order: BusinessRule, BranchingRule, VisibilityRule, SkipVisibilityRule, SkipBusinessRule, CrossSectionEnablingRule, ReEnableRule, then the shared EnableQIdsRule.
3.  Stores non-empty results per question ID in branchingRuleMap, skipBranchingRuleMap, visibilityRuleMap and skipVisibilityRuleMap.
4.  Fires only BusinessRule for every question already completed in the database, so a change on one page can raise errors on earlier pages.
5.  Returns an AgendaRuleExecutionResponse with nine collections and disposes the session in finally.
If the page being saved has its own business error, SaveAndContinueService.setAgendateResponseForValidationError empties every navigation map, so a page with an error never branches, skips or enables anything.
Rule details worth knowing
• Table rows in Sections 4 and 12 are validated by Java helpers that rules call, for example Section4InsurerValidationService and Section12CustodianValidationService, and they report through validationTableErrors with a page ID and row index.
• 8A_CrossSectionEnablingRule_Q17: when 8A (non-standard reconciliation method) is No, it enables Section 5 with resumePageId=17, status=PRESERVE and forceMandatory=true. 34A_CrossSectionEnablingRule_Q43 does the same for Section 13 and page 43.
• An earlier NullPointerException in the 8A and 34A rules was fixed by collapsing several pattern lines into one pattern with comma-separated constraints, so Drools stops evaluating as soon as a null guard fails (team notes).
• Rules still use System.out.println for tracing; these go to container stdout rather than the application logger.
7. Request lifecycle: save and continue
Every page save goes through PUT /REP/REP027/v1/saveAndContinue and one method, SaveAndContinueService.saveAndPersistToS3, which runs these steps in order. The questionId parameter can hold several IDs (one page can carry 4A and 4B), and flowType is one of guidedPermission, taskList, checkYourAnswer or permissions.
1.  Load state. Read the answer JSON from S3 (fetchExistingAnswers) and the per-section CYA flags from FIRM_DATA_ITEM_EXT (fetchCYAStatusForFirmDataItemId).
2.  Merge. mergeInput overlays the request on the stored answers and records changed fields in fieldUpdateStatusMap. A permissions save into a section whose CYA is already generated is marked UPDATED straight away.
3.  Enrich. enrichRequestWithPeriodEndDate adds the reporting period end (date rules need it); markObjectsNull clears objects the request explicitly emptied.
4.  Load journey. restService.retrieveFormJourney (DIMS) returns the section rows; their completed IDs become completedIdsFromDb.
5.  Run Drools. runAgendaGroupValidationRule fires the page's agenda groups and re-validates completed questions (section 6).
6.  Collect errors. accumulateValidationErrors merges new errors with stale ones from other sections, because Drools only fires the current page's groups. If the current page has an error, all navigation maps are cleared.
7.  Confirm deletions. If the answer would wipe data elsewhere and the user has not yet confirmed (isConfirmedForDeletion == null), createResponseForUserConfirmation returns a warning listing affected references, and nothing is saved.
8.  Mark in progress. updateTaskJson sets the section to IN PROGRESS in tasks.json.
9.  Work out next page. processAgendaResponse turns branching results into nextQIds and the CYA target.
10.  Detect guided-permission rows. If any Special row exists, or Section 1 has no row yet, the save is a special flow and specialRowName resolves to Special1, Special2 or Special3.
11.  Update references. populateReferenceStatusMap and updateReferencePart rebuild the Reference block: newly enabled questions, UPDATED flags and CYA flags.
12.  Apply skips. SkipRulesProcessingService.processSkipRulesAndDeleteFormData deletes skipped fields and hidden sections from the answers (FormDataDeletionService), prunes references (ReferencePruningService) and deletes removed sections and CSV files from the database and S3 (DatabasePruningService). Errors on skipped fields are then dropped (filterSkippedValidationErrors).
13.  Persist answers. CommonGDSService.persistToS3 writes the answer JSON.
14.  Resolve the status page. In guided permission, the next page comes from the Drools branching map, then resumePageIds, then the static flowmap.properties; otherwise from step 9.
15.  Sync the journey. For each question ID (plus any completed ID that now has an error), Rep027DbSyncService.syncAfterPersist updates the section row and any impacted sections (section 8).
16.  Update the return. FirmDataItemService.updateFirmDataItemSmart moves FIRM_DATA_ITEM.COMPLETION_STATUS through DIMS (for example first save to draft).
17.  Audit. SubmissionAsyncService.logAuditEventAsync logs the change on the asyncTaskExecutor pool.
18.  Respond. The response carries the sorted Reference block, nextQIds, validation errors and the CYA form-builder content.
Failures map to clear HTTP outcomes: unknown JSON fields and malformed JSON become 400, a missing return becomes FirmDataItemNotFoundException, and anything else is wrapped as "Failed to save REP027 data" and returned as 500 by the controller.
8. Three-way sync
The hardest part of REP027 is keeping three copies of progress consistent on every save: the answer JSON (what was answered, which references are valid, which errors stand), tasks.json (what the task list shows and where to resume) and FIRM_DATA_ITEM_EXT (which questions are completed or skipped per section). Rep027DbSyncService is the orchestrator, and S3 must be written before the database is synced.
