Submission
• SubmissionDataItemServiceImpl.saveSubmissionDataItemToS3 formats dates and writes {fdiId}_REP027.json, the payload the submission service picks up.
• getReadyToSubmitStatus reads readyToSubmitState from the answer JSON; SubmissionAsyncService.updateCompletionStatusFireAndForget moves FIRM_DATA_ITEM to Ready to Submit in the background after a clean check-answers?answerType=all.
• DCP-SCS-Submission-Service then handles submit (/submitData/{firmReferenceNo}, submitAll), resubmission requests, tracking entries and history. Audit events are written for status changes (logAuditEventsAsync).
PDF
The PDF is built in two services: dcp-sca-rep3-service shapes the data, and DCP-SCS-Utility-Service renders it.
1.  retrieveREP027ForPDF returns ResponseForPDFREP027: firm and schedule header fields plus GDSResponse[], a tree of task group → sections → questions, where each question has question, answer, options and an optional fieldset for tables.
2.  POST /utility/REP027/{language}/{version}/pdf fetches the label JSON and GLOBAL JSON from CMS, rewrites dots in label keys to underscores, and merges labels, globals and data into one JSON.
3.  It fetches the REP027 JRXML from CMS (/cms/{version}/REP027/jrxml), compiles it with JasperReports, fills it from a JsonDataSource and exports with JRPdfExporter using the sRGB ICC profile.
4.  The JRXML (REP027_Dynamic_Report, A4, FCA_VERDANA font, tagged PDF with H1–H5 headings) nests four lists: TaskGroupDS → SectionsDS → QuestionsDS → OptionsDS or FieldSetDS.
The PDF is also produced for the No Data and guided-permission scenarios (team notes). Platform-wide, 267 Jasper reports move to JasperReports 7.0.7 as part of the migration.
